From 30717e34a112da05f880a0ca0c5ba139ce7be4de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:26:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: public suffixes from our own list reader, not libpsl

PublicSuffixStore's two platform calls (is a name a public suffix, and
what is its registrable domain) are answered by PublicSuffixAmiga.c in
place of PublicSuffixStoreCurl.cpp and libpsl. It reads Mozilla's Public
Suffix List once, from PROGDIR:Network/public-suffixes (then
ENVARC:OpenBrowser/public-suffixes), as openamigabrowser's
tools/psl-compile.py writes it: one rule a line, names in Punycode,
sorted, so the file is searched as it is. The lookup is the list's own
algorithm: an exception rule wins, then the longest rule, then "*" for
the registrable domain only. "ck" is a suffix when "*.ck" is a rule, as
libpsl had it. Without the file nothing is a public suffix and a name's
site is its last two labels, and the engine says so once on stderr.

libpsl is no longer found or linked. A newer list needs no new engine.
---
 Source/WebCore/PlatformAmiga.cmake            |  12 ++
 .../network/amiga/PublicSuffixAmiga.c         | 201 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../network/amiga/PublicSuffixAmiga.h         |  30 +++
 .../network/amiga/PublicSuffixStoreAmiga.cpp  |  46 ++++
 Source/cmake/OptionsAmiga.cmake               |   1 -
 5 files changed, 289 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/PublicSuffixAmiga.c
 create mode 100644 Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/PublicSuffixAmiga.h
 create mode 100644 Source/WebCore/platform/network/amiga/PublicSuffixStoreAmiga.cpp

